    "title": "Happy Opening Day—Here’s how to watch Pirates vs. Mets live for free",
    "text": "New York Post may be compensated and/or receive an affiliate commission if you click or buy through our links. Featured pricing is subject to change. An image collage containing 2 images, Image 1 shows Mar 21, 2026; Bradenton, Florida, USA; Pittsburgh Pirates starting pitcher Paul Skenes (30) during the first inning against the Toronto Blue Jays at LECOM Park. Mandatory Credit: Kim Klement Neitzel-Imagn Images, Image 2 shows Francisco Lindor wearing a New York Mets uniform, helmet, and orange batting gloves, holding a batIt’s been a long offseason, but the wait is finally over — MLB Opening Day is here, and it’s kicking off with the Pirates and Mets facing off in Queens.The Mets had a fairly active offseason after parting ways with Pete Alonso, Brandon Nimmo and Edwin Diaz. Some notable pickups include pitcher Freddy Peralta (who starts today), infielders Bo Bichette and Jorge Polanco, and former Yankee Luke Weaver.The Pirates also added to their roster during the offseason by trading for All-Star second baseman Brandon Lowe and signing 1B/OF Ryan O’Hearn.pirates vs. mets: what to knowWhen: March 26, 1:15 p.m. ETWhere: Citi Field (Flushing, New York)Channel: NBCStreaming: DIRECTV (try it free)Today’s game will kick off a new era of MLB on NBC. The network will broadcast over 60 games during the 2026-27 season, beginning with Pirates vs. Mets.The teams will be off tomorrow, before resuming the three-game series on Friday and Saturday.Pirates vs. Mets Opening Day start timeFirst pitch at the Pirates vs. Mets game is scheduled for 1:15 p.m. ET today, March 26.How to watch Pirates vs. Mets for freeIf you don’t have cable, you’ll need a live TV streaming service to stream MLB Opening Day for free. Today’s Mets game is a national game airing on NBC, meaning it will not be on SNY.DIRECTV is our favorite service for watching TV live for free — it has a five-day free trial and there are a ton of options for plans that include NBC, including genre packs that offer more flexibility at lower price points. NBC is part of the MyNews genre pack ($39.99/month and the MySports ($44.99/month for a limited time) genre pack.TRY DIRECTV FOR FREEYou can also catch every minute of the Olympics with a subscription to Peacock, which starts at $10.99/month.Pirates vs. Mets starting pitchersNew Mets ace Freddy Peralta will be on the mound for the home team. The Mets acquired Peralta in a trade with Milwaukee, and he’s set to make his third straight Opening Day start.Reigning NL Cy Young winner Paul Skenes will start his second straight Opening Day for the Pirates.Why Trust Post Wanted by the New York PostThis article was written by Angela Tricarico, Commerce Streaming Reporter for Post Wanted Shopping, Page Six, and Decider.com. Angela keeps readers up to date with cord-cutter-friendly deals, and information on how to watch your favorite sports teams, TV shows, and movies on every streaming service. Not only does Angela test and compare the streaming services she writes about to ensure readers are getting the best prices, but she’s also a superfan specializing in the intersection of shopping, tech, sports, and pop culture. When she’s not writing about (or watching) TV, movies, and sports, she’s also keeping up on the underrated perfume dupes at Bath & Body Works and testing headphones. Prior to joining Decider and The New York Post in 2023, she wrote about streaming and consumer tech at Insider Reviews.",
